('Series vs Parallel Circuits','diagram','Physics','Electricity',NULL,ARRAY['Form 3','Form 4','O-Level','IGCSE','Grade 10','Grade 11','Form 5','Form 6','A-Level','Grade 12'],'https://placehold.co/320x400/0e1d47/ffffff?text=Physics%0ADiagram','Two circuits with identical lamps: one series, one parallel, with ammeter/voltmeter placements and the current/voltage rules.','{"version": 1, "title": "Series vs Parallel Circuits", "caption": "Two circuits with identical lamps: one series, one parallel, with ammeter/voltmeter placements and the current/voltage rules.", "subject": "Physics", "topic": "Electricity", "elements": [{"label": "Series circuit", "role": "components in a single loop"}, {"label": "Parallel circuit", "role": "components on separate branches"}, {"label": "Current in series", "role": "SAME everywhere: I = I1 = I2"}, {"label": "Current in parallel", "role": "SPLITS: I = I1 + I2"}, {"label": "Voltage in series", "role": "SHARED: V = V1 + V2"}, {"label": "Voltage in parallel", "role": "SAME across each branch"}, {"label": "Ammeter", "role": "always connected in series"}, {"label": "Voltmeter", "role": "always connected in parallel"}, {"label": "Resistance in series", "role": "adds: R = R1 + R2"}, {"label": "Resistance in parallel", "role": "1/R = 1/R1 + 1/R2 (total is LESS than the smallest)"}], "relationships": ["One broken lamp kills a series circuit but not a parallel one — why homes are wired in parallel", "Ohm''s law V = IR applies to each component and to the whole circuit"], "depth_notes": {"JC": "Build both circuits and state what happens when one lamp breaks.", "O-Level": "Apply all the current/voltage/resistance rules and Ohm''s law numerically.", "A-Level": "Extend to EMF vs terminal p.d., internal resistance and potential dividers."}, "style": "studysync-edu-v1"}'::jsonb),
